// D9772's generic face: a generic function whose parameter is a nullable function over the type
// parameter, delivered at one function type and called through it with a closure and `null`.
// fn-value-generic-nullable-fn-param-open is the twin that leaves the type parameter open.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function g<T>(f: ((x: T) => T) | null, x: T): T {
  if f != null { return f(x) }
  x
}
// @@VALUE@@
g
// @@TYPE@@
(f: ((x: i32) => i32) | null, x: i32) => i32
// @@PROOF@@
print(v((x: i32) => x + 1, 2) * 10 + v(null, 5))
// @@WANT@@
35
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a function, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
